      "content": "For partial year depreciation, you calculate the fractional part of the useful life that has elapsed, which in this case would be 8 months out of 12, or 2/3. \n\n1. Calculate the partial year depreciation: $5,000 x 2/3 = $3,333\n2. You'd record this as a direct cost on your income statement for the first year.\n\nThe annual depreciation figure of $5,000 remains the same, but the actual amount you'd expense in the first year is reduced due to the physical usage.",
